LC 567 — Permutation in String
Pattern:Sliding Window

Algorithm

Take a window of size s1.length().
Count characters in s1 and the window.
Move the window one step at a time.
If counts match → true.

CODE:
class Solution {
public:
    bool checkInclusion(string s1, string s2) {
        if (s1.size() > s2.size()) return false;

        int a[26]={}, b[26]={};
        for (char c:s1) a[c-'a']++;

        for (int i=0;i<s2.size();i++) {
            b[s2[i]-'a']++;
            if (i >= s1.size())
                b[s2[i-s1.size()]-'a']--;

            if (i >= s1.size()-1 && equal(a,a+26,b))
                return true;
        }
        return false;
    }
};

EX:
s1 = "ab"
s2 = "eidbaooo"

Window: "ei" ❌
Window: "id" ❌
Window: "db" ❌
Window: "ba" ✅

"ba" is a permutation of "ab"
Answer = true
